{"title":"Find The Sum Of Subsequence Powers","difficulty":"Hard","statement":"You are given an integer array nums of length n, and a positive integer k.\nThe power of a subsequence is defined as the minimum absolute difference between any two elements in the subsequence.\nReturn the sum of powers of all subsequences of nums which have length equal to k.\nSince the answer may be large, return it modulo 10^9 + 7.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: nums = [1,2,3,4], k = 3\nOutput: 4\n```\n\nThere are 4 subsequences in nums which have length 3: [1,2,3], [1,3,4], [1,2,4], and [2,3,4]. The sum of powers is |2 - 3| + |3 - 4| + |2 - 1| + |3 - 4| = 4.\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: nums = [2,2], k = 2\nOutput: 0\n```\n\nThe only subsequence in nums which has length 2 is [2,2]. The sum of powers is |2 - 2| = 0.\n\n### Example 3\n\n```text\nInput: nums = [4,3,-1], k = 2\nOutput: 10\n```\n\nThere are 3 subsequences in nums which have length 2: [4,3], [4,-1], and [3,-1]. The sum of powers is |4 - 3| + |4 - (-1)| + |3 - (-1)| = 10.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 2 <= n == nums.length <= 50\n- -10^8 <= nums[i] <= 10^8\n- 2 <= k <= n\n","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def sumOfPowers(self, nums: List[int], k: int) -> int:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().sumOfPowers","parameters":[{"name":"nums","type":"List[int]"},{"name":"k","type":"int"}],"returnType":"int","tests":[{"input":[[-1,-10,12,26],3],"expected":45},{"input":[[-1,-14,-23,7],3],"expected":34},{"input":[[-1,-14,4,-20,30,-2,-5,-30,-24,-30,-24],7],"expected":249},{"input":[[-1,-2,-23,-25,-25,-15,-24,22,18],4],"expected":297},{"input":[[-1,-23,-14,8,-10,-14,-14,16,-12],8],"expected":0},{"input":[[-1,-25,-14,2,-12,14,1,-4,22,-10],8],"expected":63},{"input":[[-1,-27,10,14,3,12,11,5],7],"expected":9},{"input":[[-1,0,-25,8,-13],4],"expected":20},{"input":[[-1,1,12,-21,15,-21,-27,28],2],"expected":666},{"input":[[-1,11,-22,8,3,-25,-14,30,-24,15,-24,-13],2],"expected":1414},{"input":[[-1,14,-26,-29,-18,8